ent-ClothingOuterLeathercoat = coat of the commander
    .desc = A coat of plates concealed beneath a heavy leather surcoat. Only the most battle-hardened of Azuria's commanders can hope to bear its burden, both metaphorically and quite literally.

ent-ClothingOuterHalfplate = steel half-plate
    .desc = A padded steel cuirass, adorned with segmented pauldrons. Its prevalence amongst the pious is indisputable - deceptively light, sturdy, and accomadating to a Cleric's miracle-casting gestures.

ent-ClothingOuterIronplate = iron plate armor
    .desc = A 'munition'-grade set of iron plate armor, fitted with pauldrons and tassets for additional coverage. Most of these sets, produced within the last century, can trace their origins to an edict from Hammerhold's former King: one which demanded a munitions run, but forgot to specify its tailoring towards the dwarven physique. ‎ 'Slow to don-and-doff, without a trusted Levyman's aid..

ent-ClothingOuterPlateHarness = plate armor
    .desc = A pristine set of steel plate armor, fitted with tassets and bracers for additional coverage. To the Knights of Psydonia, these sets are a symbolic manifestation of their oath; to serve thine kingdom without hesitation, and to rebuke all the villains who'd dare to defile it. ‎ 'Slow to don-and-doff, without a trusted Squire's aid..

ent-ClothingOuterSteelCuirass = steel cuirass
    .desc = A steel cuirass. It bears all the hallmarks of sixteenth-century nobility: angularity, polishedness, and - above all else - class.
